### Talaria Stack Light -- API test collection
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### and click "Send Request" above any block below.
###
### If mDNS isn't resolving on your network, replace @host with the
### device's DHCP IP (printed on the serial monitor at boot).
###
### Set @apiKey to the API_KEY value from include/secrets.h -- every
### POST/DELETE below needs it (X-Api-Key header) or comes back 401.

@host = talaria-stack-01.local
@base = http://{{host}}
@apiKey = change-me

### Health check (no auth required)
GET {{base}}/health

### Current status (no auth required)
GET {{base}}/status

### Set status: open (green solid)
POST {{base}}/status/open
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Set status: closed (red solid)
POST {{base}}/status/closed
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Set status: warning (yellow slow flash)
POST {{base}}/status/warning
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Set status: critical (red fast flash)
POST {{base}}/status/critical
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Set status: offline (yellow fast flash) -- manual test only, normally
### the device sets this itself when it loses contact with Talaria
POST {{base}}/status/offline
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Run the light bench self-test: cycles red -> yellow -> green
### (~700ms each), then restores whatever status was active before it
POST {{base}}/test/cycle
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Hold all three lights on until told otherwise (e.g. to check every
### relay energizes, or total current draw)
POST {{base}}/test/all-on
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Turn all lights back off (cancels the all-on test)
POST {{base}}/test/all-off
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### List all active structured conditions (no auth required)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/signals

### Post a structured condition -- multiple can be active at once (keyed
### by source + condition); the light shows whichever is highest-severity
POST {{base}}/api/v1/signals
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "printer-front-01",
  "condition": "PAPER_JAM",
  "severity": "warning",
  "message": "Front printer is jammed",
  "ttlSeconds": 300
}

### A second, higher-severity condition from a different source -- the
### light should switch to this one while the printer jam stays queued
POST {{base}}/api/v1/signals
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "network",
  "condition": "LINK_DOWN",
  "severity": "critical",
  "message": "Ethernet link lost"
}

### Clear the network condition -- light should drop back to the printer
### jam (still active), not all the way back to the base status
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/signals/network/LINK_DOWN
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Clear the printer condition too -- light should drop back to the base
### status (whatever /status/* was last set to)
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/signals/printer-front-01/PAPER_JAM
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Heartbeat -- Talaria should call this periodically (well under
### HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS) even when nothing has changed. If nothing at
### all arrives (this, a /status/* call, or an /api/v1/signals
### post/delete) within the timeout, the display forces itself to
### offline on its own -- try waiting past it and re-running GET /status
POST {{base}}/heartbeat
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Missing/wrong API key -- should come back as a 401 JSON error
POST {{base}}/status/open

### Invalid severity -- should come back as a 400 JSON error
POST {{base}}/api/v1/signals
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "test", "condition": "BAD_SEVERITY", "severity": "not-a-real-severity" }

### ttlSeconds beyond MAX_TTL_SECONDS -- should come back as a 400 JSON error
POST {{base}}/api/v1/signals
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "test", "condition": "TTL_TOO_LONG", "severity": "info", "ttlSeconds": 99999999 }

### Post a short-lived condition, then check it's gone after ~6s (see
### "expiresInMs" in the response and in GET /api/v1/signals meanwhile)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/signals
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "test", "condition": "SHORT_LIVED", "severity": "warning", "ttlSeconds": 5 }

### Unknown route -- should come back as a 404 JSON error, not a hang
GET {{base}}/nope

### Dashboard -- open {{base}}/ directly in a browser instead of here
